From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:11:13 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 41/45] inkling2: grouped experts on the family's own kernels,
 no empty tiles and the same bits

Prompt chunks list each expert's members in runs (an item list) instead of launching a tile for
every possible 16-row group, and wide calls take 32 members by 64 columns a block. Each output keeps
main's k order, splits and warp sums, so z, xd and the layer output are bit-identical to
tf_exl3_grouped_2 (harness checksums at 1 to 2,048 rows). Harness, one rank, 2,048 rows: grouped
gate/up + down 57.7 -> 20.9 ms a layer; 1 row 182 -> 174 us.
